+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report: `vte` 0.15.0
+
+Tests were added with `hegeltest` 0.28.2 (`cargo add --dev hegeltest --ignore-rust-version`;
+the crate pins `rust-version = 1.62.1`, below hegeltest's MSRV of 1.86).
+
+Test locations follow the skill's "modify existing test files" rule:
+
+- `src/lib.rs` (existing `mod tests`) — 10 parser properties
+- `src/params.rs` (new `#[cfg(test)] mod tests`; the file had none) — 2 `Params` properties
+- `src/ansi.rs` (existing `mod tests`, `ansi` + `std` features) — 1 `Processor` property
+
+## Properties tested
+
+| # | Property | Test | Evidence |
+|---|----------|------|----------|
+| 1 | `Parser::advance` never panics on arbitrary bytes fed in arbitrary chunks through one reused parser | `tests::advance_never_panics_on_arbitrary_chunked_input` | Parse robustness (Tier 1): the parser consumes untrusted PTY data; docs say it implements the DEC ANSI state machine which is total over all bytes |
+| 2 | Feeding input in arbitrary chunks produces exactly the same dispatch sequence as feeding it whole | `tests::chunked_advance_equals_whole_input_advance` | The `partial_utf8` buffer exists solely for this; existing unit tests `partial_utf8`, `partial_invalid_utf8`, `partial_utf8_separating_utf8` assert specific instances |
+| 3 | `Perform::print` never receives C0/C1 control characters | `tests::print_never_receives_control_chars` | `Perform::execute` doc: "Execute a C0 or C1 control function"; `ground_dispatch` routes `\x00..=\x1f` and `\u{80}..=\u{9f}` to `execute` |
+| 4 | `Perform::execute` only receives C0/C1 control bytes | `tests::execute_only_receives_control_bytes` | Same doc contract, opposite direction |
+| 5 | A well-formed CSI sequence (arbitrary params/subparams within `MAX_PARAMS`, optional private marker, ≤2 intermediates, final byte `0x40..=0x7E`) round-trips into exactly one `csi_dispatch` with that data and `ignore == false` | `tests::csi_roundtrip` | Generalizes existing unit tests `parse_csi_*`, `csi_subparameters`, `esc_reset`; state-machine byte ranges in `advance_csi_*` |
+| 6 | An OSC sequence with arbitrary parameter byte strings round-trips into one `osc_dispatch` with those params and the right `bell_terminated` flag | `tests::osc_roundtrip` | Generalizes `parse_osc`, `osc_bell_terminated`, `osc_c0_st_terminated`, `osc_containing_string_terminator` |
+| 7 | Numeric CSI params saturate at `u16::MAX` for arbitrary `u64` values, leading zeros irrelevant | `tests::csi_param_saturates_at_u16_max` | `action_paramnext` uses `saturating_mul`/`saturating_add`; unit test `parse_long_csi_param` checks one instance |
+| 8 | DCS callback protocol: `put`/`unhook` only occur between `hook` and its matching `unhook`; hooks never nest | `tests::dcs_hook_put_unhook_protocol` | `Perform::hook`/`put`/`unhook` docs describe this handler lifecycle |
+| 9 | Dispatched data respects documented size limits: ≤ `MAX_PARAMS` (sub)params, ≤ `MAX_INTERMEDIATES` intermediates, ≤ `MAX_OSC_PARAMS` OSC params, CSI action char in `0x40..=0x7E`, no empty subparam slices | `tests::dispatched_data_respects_size_limits` | The `MAX_*` constants plus the `ignore`-flag documentation on `csi_dispatch`/`hook` |
+| 10 | `advance_until_terminated` is equivalent to `advance`: terminating at arbitrary points and resuming with the remaining bytes yields the same total dispatch sequence | `tests::advance_until_terminated_resumes_to_same_dispatches` | Method doc: "This is equivalent to `Self::advance`, but stops when..."; `#[must_use]` note says the return value is for processing remaining bytes |
+| 11 | `Params` agrees with a `Vec<Vec<u16>>` model under every `push`/`extend`/`clear` sequence (stateful model test, `#[hegel::state_machine]`), including `len`/`is_empty` consistency | `params::tests::params_agree_with_model` | Model test (Tier 1); operations guarded by `is_full` exactly as at all call sites in `lib.rs` |
+| 12 | `ParamsIter::size_hint` satisfies the `Iterator` contract: lower bound ≤ items yielded ≤ upper bound | `params::tests::params_iter_size_hint_is_consistent` | std `Iterator::size_hint` documented contract |
+| 13 | `ansi::Processor::advance` never panics and always makes progress on arbitrary chunked bytes with synchronized-update escapes (BSU/ESU) mixed in | `ansi::tests::processor_advance_never_panics` | Feature-flag testing (`ansi` is non-default); the `advance` loop plus sync buffering (`advance_sync`) is the crate's most intricate control flow |
